                      "name": "ticket",
                      "prefix": "Ticket:",
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  ],
                  "instructions": "Assign the support ticket to the squad that owns it: atlas, harbor, beacon, or quill.\n\nPlease adhere to the following rules when making your prediction:\n1. Route to **atlas** when the ticket concerns billing, invoices, charges, or subscription management (e.g., duplicate charges, incorrect invoice details, billing cycle changes, or cancellation disputes).\n\n2. Route to **harbor** when the ticket describes an active technical outage, system error, or degraded performance (e.g., API errors, slow load times, failed webhook delivery, or broken transactional emails following a deploy).\n\n3. Route to **beacon** when the ticket involves authentication or account access issues, including login failures, locked accounts, password resets, two-factor authentication problems, or unauthorized access concerns.\n\n4. Route to **quill** when the ticket is a feature request, product improvement suggestion, or integration idea with no urgent technical or billing component.\n\n5. Route to **quill** when the ticket asks a \"how do I\" or general usage question about product functionality, onboarding, or available API capabilities.\n\n6. Distinguish **harbor** from **atlas** for payment-related tickets: if the issue is a system-level payment processing failure (e.g., checkout timeouts affecting all users), route to **harbor**; if it is an individual billing discrepancy or invoice record issue, route to **atlas**.\n\n7. Distinguish **harbor** from **beacon** for email-related tickets: if users are not receiving system-generated emails due to a technical failure (e.g., no receipt emails since a deploy), route to **harbor**; if an unexpected security email was received (e.g., an unrequested password reset), route to **beacon**.\n\n8. Route to **beacon** when the ticket involves access control or security anomalies, such as a former employee retaining workspace access or suspicious account activity, even if no active login failure is reported.",
                  "metadata": {},
                  "outputs": [
